---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Downloader from '../components/Downloader.astro';
import AdPlaceholder from '../components/AdPlaceholder.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Download YouTube Videos HD 1080p, 720p — YTD Local"
  description="High-definition YouTube video downloader. Download 1080p, 720p, and 480p videos directly to your device with fast local companion processing."
>
  <div class="page-wrapper">
    <section class="downloader-section">
      <Downloader />
    </section>

    <AdPlaceholder slotLocation="seo-top" />

    <article class="seo-article">
      <h1>YouTube Video Downloader HD (1080p & 720p)</h1>
      <p>
        YTD Local allows you to download videos from YouTube in full high-definition resolution directly onto your computer or mobile device. By utilizing your machine's local processing capability via <code>yt-dlp</code> and <code>FFmpeg</code>, YTD Local bypasses slow third-party servers and cloud queues.
      </p>

      <h2>Key Benefits of HD Video Downloads</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>1080p Full HD & 60fps Support:</strong> Experience pristine video quality with high frame rate support.</li>
        <li><strong>Original Audio Quality:</strong> Merges video and audio streams seamlessly using local FFmpeg processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Private & Secure:</strong> No tracking cookies, no server logs, and zero middleman cloud storage.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Supported Video Formats & Quality Levels</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the original upload quality, YTD Local supports extracting video in 1080p, 720p, 480p, 360p, as well as standalone MP3 audio format.
      </p>

      <AdPlaceholder slotLocation="seo-mid" />

      <h2>How to Download HD Videos Locally</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Copy the link of the video you wish to download.</li>
        <li>Paste the URL into the YTD Local search box above and click <strong>Analyze</strong>.</li>
        <li>Select 1080p or your preferred quality.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Download</strong> to start local processing directly to your Downloads folder.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-wrapper {
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 24px;
  }

  .seo-article {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 48px auto;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .seo-article h1 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .seo-article h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-top: 32px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .seo-article p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .seo-article ul, .seo-article ol {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    padding-left: 24px;
  }

  .seo-article li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
